{
    "background_story": "Matthias was a devout and compassionate bishop who lived in the 10th century. He was appointed to oversee the eparchy of a small, rural region in Eastern Europe. Despite the challenges of serving a scattered and impoverished community, Matthias worked tirelessly to establish schools, hospitals, and churches. He traveled extensively throughout his eparchy, often on foot, to minister to the spiritual needs of his flock. Matthias was particularly devoted to the care of the poor and the marginalized, and his selfless service earned him great respect and admiration. Under his guidance, the eparchy flourished, becoming a beacon of hope and faith in a time of great turmoil. Matthias' legacy as a wise and compassionate leader continued to inspire generations of clergy and laity alike.",
